{"duration_api_ms":122468,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"e2365500-789f-4585-8b95-7419838f80c8","total_cost_usd":0.9936425999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":48,"cache_creation_input_tokens":51187,"cache_read_input_tokens":1583473,"output_tokens":13363,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1961},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":51187,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1159,"cache_read_input_tokens":82154,"cache_creation_input_tokens":417,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":417},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":48,"outputTokens":13363,"cacheReadInputTokens":1583473,"cacheCreationInputTokens":51187,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.9936425999999999,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":1961,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":51187,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":24,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I've landed the PKT-0080 lookup-table change for `hb_get_script_horizontal_direction` on the sdkjs branch pkt/PKT-0084, with a unit test and a browser measurement. All four acceptance commands pass.\n\n**What changed**\n- **The change:** in `common/libfont/common.js` the old switch stays as a reference function. At load it fills a `Map` with the scripts that are not left-to-right, and the main function takes a shortcut for Latin and Common text. It is committed in sdkjs as `42c8391`. The patch in the PKT-0080 log no longer applied with `git apply`, so I made the same change by hand.\n- **Unit test:** the new `tests/common/libfont/script-direction.{html,js}` checks that the table gives the same direction as the switch for every `HB_SCRIPT` value, plus a few known scripts and values that are not scripts at all (0, -1, null and so on). The sdkjs-common oracle picks it up automatically: 14/14 assertions.\n- **Acceptance results:**\n\n  | Command | Result |\n  |---|---|\n  | `sdkjs-common` | 7/7 suites |\n  | `sdkjs-word` | 42/42 suites |\n  | `differential/sdkjs-word` | PASS |\n  | `differential/sdkjs-common` | PASS |\n\n**Browser measurement**\nI opened large-100p.docx three times each in the running Document Server, once with the original sdkjs build and once with this branch's build, and profiled the CPU. The function's own time dropped from about 20–36 ms to about 0–6 ms, which matches PKT-0080's estimate. The total open times also differ, but that comparison isn't fair: the original build is the unminified fallback (minifying ran out of memory) and the new one is minified. Only the per-function number reflects this change.\n\n**Decisions**\n- I didn't use `profile-fonts.js`, which exists only on pkt/PKT-0072 and measures the installed bundle. I didn't build a mirror of the install either. Instead, Playwright swapped `/sdkjs/word/sdk-all{,-min}.js` for the two builds the differential oracle had already made.\n- That A/B script is not committed, because the packet allows no new files. It is in `/tmp/claude-0/-home-claude-euro-office-server-theseus-worktrees-PKT-0084/e2365500-789f-4585-8b95-7419838f80c8/scratchpad/ab.cjs`, and the method is described in the Executor log.\n\n**Problem found and follow-up requested**\n`.theseus/oracle/differential/build.sh` crashes with exit 123 whenever the sdkjs checkout has untracked files: it computes their checksums from the wrong directory. I got around it by committing in sdkjs first. I filed a follow-up request in `.theseus/spawn/PKT-0084-fix-differential-build-sh-hashing-of-untracked-f.md` (requires `documentserver` and `browser`).\n\nThe Executor log, Lessons for the Atlas and friction line are written, and `theseus validate` reports no errors. Everything is committed as `6c6a73c`.\n\n**Lessons for the Atlas**\n- You can A/B-test an sdkjs change in the browser by routing `sdk-all.js` to builds from the differential oracle, with no mirror of the install. First check that both builds are minified, or that neither is.\n- Commit in `external/sdkjs` before running the differential oracles whenever there are new untracked files.","ttft_ms":1885,"type":"result","duration_ms":815296,"uuid":"ebd91aa4-0975-4011-94b3-6324ad987440","ttft_stream_ms":1091,"time_to_request_ms":329,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":6,"system_prompt":185,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":30,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":10,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":7,"init_frame_send":4,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":4,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":15,"query_setup":4,"auto_mode_context_wait":8,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":24,"message_normalization":3,"client_creation":7,"request_build":11},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":118,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":180,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":206,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":136,"process_rss_mib_result":241,"process_anon_mib_result":150,"process_peak_rss_mib":254,"process_cpu_ms_turn":18426,"process_wall_ms_turn":815295,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":2340,"process_wall_ms_streaming":99962,"main_stream_count":24,"main_stream_event_count":1876,"main_stream_chunk_count":1434,"